		},
		{
			"id":"6a9768c36ce3ba7a",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"classifier node",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":63,
			"y":720,
			"width":243,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"0b80336999c8559a",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"```mermaid\ngraph TD;\n\t__start__([start]):::first\n\tcomprehend(comprehend)\n\tgeneral_reply([\"general_reply<br/><small><em>LLM generated</em></small>\"])\n\tout_of_scope_reply([\"out_of_scope_reply<br/><small><em>static, no LLM</em></small>\"])\n\tplanner(planner)\n\tplan_approval([\"plan_approval <br> <small><em>interrupt, HITL</em></small>\"]):::hitl\n\twave_barrier(wave_barrier)\n\tupdate_ledger(update_ledger)\n\tsynthesizer(synthesizer)\n\t__end__([__end__]):::last\n\n\t__start__ --> comprehend;\n\tcomprehend -.->|general| general_reply;\n\tcomprehend -.->|out of scope| out_of_scope_reply;\n\tcomprehend -.->|complex| planner;\n\tgeneral_reply --> __end__;\n\tout_of_scope_reply --> __end__;\n\tplanner --> plan_approval;\n\tplan_approval -.->|Send: ready task| crm__start__;\n\tplan_approval -.->|Send: ready task| billing__start__;\n\tplan_approval -.->|no tasks| synthesizer;\n\tcrm__end__ --> wave_barrier;\n\tbilling__end__ --> wave_barrier;\n\twave_barrier -.->|next wave| crm__start__;\n\twave_barrier -.->|next wave| billing__start__;\n\twave_barrier -.->|done| update_ledger;\n\tupdate_ledger --> synthesizer;\n\tsynthesizer --> __end__;\n\n\tsubgraph crm [crm domain agent]\n\tcrm__start__([start])\n\tcrm_model(model)\n\tcrm_tools(tools)\n\tcrm__end__([end])\n\tcrm__start__ --> crm_model;\n\tcrm_model -.->|no tool call| crm__end__;\n\tcrm_model -.->|call tool| crm_tools;\n\tcrm_tools -.-> crm_model;\n\tend\n\n\tsubgraph billing [billing domain agent]\n\tbilling__start__([start])\n\tbilling_model(model)\n\tbilling_tools(tools)\n\tbilling_hitl([\"HumanInTheLoopMiddleware<br/><small><em>refund_customer only</em></small>\"]):::hitl\n\tbilling__end__([end])\n\tbilling__start__ --> billing_model;\n\tbilling_model --> billing_hitl;\n\tbilling_hitl -.->|auto-approved tool| billing_tools;\n\tbilling_hitl -.->|no tool call| billing__end__;\n\tbilling_hitl -.->|flagged: needs approval| billing_hitl;\n\tbilling_tools -.-> billing_model;\n\tend\n```",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-680,
			"y":1380,
			"width":1320,
			"height":1540
		},
		{
			"id":"bbbab04bfb692428",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"## claude conversation\n\n[Multiagent pattern design with LangGraph](https://claude.ai/share/aa82280c-fc86-4524-8542-250f559dbefc \"https://claude.ai/share/aa82280c-fc86-4524-8542-250f559dbefc\")",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-762,
			"y":-80,
			"width":498,
			"height":120
		},
		{
			"id":"6a4845cc0d53e883",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"general",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":427,
			"y":460,
			"width":243,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"b6f8ce73bbd7517a",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"out of scope",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":427,
			"y":540,
			"width":243,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"51764361398a4efe",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Scoped domain asks",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":427,
			"y":720,
			"width":243,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"22eb66830ddf3a9f",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Gap",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":407,
			"y":1010,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"0a8e122bef4de7db",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Imapct",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":407,
			"y":1090,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"515692b10619de2c",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Risk",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":407,
			"y":934,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"c175e2998298b737",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"specialized tools (API, external to the system)",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1447,
			"y":420,
			"width":243,
			"height":100
		},
		{
			"id":"ee3771af7d2109c9",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**\"Wave\"** = one round of tasks that are all simultaneously ready to run (nothing they depend on is still pending), dispatched together via `Send()`. In the `t1/t2/t3` example from before:\n\n- **Wave 1**: `t1` and `t3` have no dependencies → both dispatch immediately, in parallel.\n- **Wave 2**: `t2` depends on `t1` → it can't go out until wave 1 finishes and `t1` is marked done.\n\n**\"wave_barrier\"** is a plain no-op node whose only job is to be the single place that decides \"what's the next wave\" — after _every_ parallel branch from the current wave has funneled through it. It's not doing work; it exists purely as a join point.\n\nThe reason it has to exist, concretely, is the bug from a few turns back: my first attempt let each parallel branch decide the next wave _on its own_, right after it finished. With `t1` and `t3` both finishing in wave 1, that meant \"what's next\" got computed **twice** — once by the `t1` branch, once by the `t3` branch — and both computations independently saw \"`t2`'s dependency is satisfied now\" and both dispatched it. `t2` ran three times instead of once. Routing everyone through one shared node before the decision is made is what stops that.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":920,
			"y":1840,
			"width":1100,
			"height":440
		},
		{
			"id":"4e2c75f6b74ebf77",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"### Planner Node. \n1. llm with structured output for the next\n2. plan approval pause (HITL)\n3. scope on how much sub agents can it call\n\t1. 3 to 5\n\t2. parallel or independent scope down is needed\n4. Individual agent failure retry (max 3 times)",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":954,
			"y":570,
			"width":373,
			"height":350
		},
		{
			"id":"ebcb031d8b6b7861",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"### Individual Agents (speciallized) - N\n1. tool fail retry\n2. scoped custom prompt\n3. Risk tool call approval",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1447,
			"y":600,
			"width":336,
			"height":281
		},
